>> title: Mango Pudding
>> category: Custards & Puddings
>> tags: mango, gelatin, no-bake, chilled, dim sum
>> counters: Dim Sum Counter
>> aka: 芒果布甸, mong gwo bou din
>> servings: 8
>> time: 4 hr 30 min
>> slack: narrow — the gelatin is bloomed cold and dissolved in warm rather than boiling liquid, because boiled gelatin sets weak and a pudding that will not turn out cannot be re-set; the four hours in the fridge after that ask nothing of you
>> step.1: bloom 5 min
>> step.3: whisk in the gelatin

Sprinkle @unflavored gelatin{2%Tbs}(21 g, three envelopes) over @cold water{1/2%cup}(120 mL) and let it bloom for ~{5%min}.

Dissolve @granulated sugar{1/2%cup}(100 g) in @boiling water{1/2%cup}(120 mL).

Whisk @&(~2)bloomed gelatin{} into @&(~1)hot syrup{}.

Puree @ripe mango{2%lb}(900 g; about 3 large, peeled and cubed), @lime juice{1%Tbs}(15 mL) in a #blender{} until smooth.

Blend @&(~1)mango puree{} with @&(~2)gelatin syrup{}, @evaporated milk{1/2%cup}(120 mL), @heavy cream{1/2%cup}(120 mL).

Pour @&(~1)pudding{} into #8 cups{} and chill for ~{4%hr} until set.
